---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import MedalBadge from '../../components/MedalBadge.astro';

const allSystems = await getCollection('systems');

// Define the ARM family systems
const systemARMSlugs = [
  'acorn-archimedes'
];

const systems = systemARMSlugs
  .map(slug => allSystems.find(s => s.slug === slug))
  .filter(Boolean)
  .filter(s => s.data.status !== 'vault')
  .sort((a, b) => {
    const tierOrder = { platinum: 0, gold: 1, silver: 2, bronze: 3 };
    const tierA = tierOrder[a.data.medal_tier] ?? 4;
    const tierB = tierOrder[b.data.medal_tier] ?? 4;
    if (tierA !== tierB) return tierA - tierB;
    return (b.data.total_lessons || 0) - (a.data.total_lessons || 0);
  });

const totalLessons = systems.reduce((sum, s) => sum + (s.data.total_lessons || 0), 0);
const totalGames = systems.reduce((sum, s) => sum + (s.data.total_games || 0), 0);

// Group by medal tier
const platinum = systems.filter(s => s.data.medal_tier === 'platinum');
const gold = systems.filter(s => s.data.medal_tier === 'gold');
const silver = systems.filter(s => s.data.medal_tier === 'silver');
const bronze = systems.filter(s => s.data.medal_tier === 'bronze');
---

<Layout title="ARM Architecture Track | Code Like It's 198x">
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-900 to-black text-green-400">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-12">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
          <a href="/tracks/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-green-400 transition">
            ← Back to Tracks
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
          <div class="text-6xl">🏛️</div>
          <div>
            <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold mb-2 text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-red-400 to-pink-400">
              ARM RISC Architecture
            </h1>
            <p class="text-xl text-gray-300">
              The elegant RISC processor that revolutionized computing
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 mb-12">
        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-700">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">{systems.length}</div>
          <div class="text-gray-400">Systems</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-700">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">{totalLessons.toLocaleString()}</div>
          <div class="text-gray-400">Total Lessons</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-700">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">{totalGames.toLocaleString()}</div>
          <div class="text-gray-400">Games to Build</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-700">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">1987-Present</div>
          <div class="text-gray-400">Era Covered</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-8 mb-12 border-2 border-gray-700">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">About the ARM Architecture</h2>
        <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-gray-300">
          <p class="mb-4">
            ARM (originally Acorn RISC Machine) began in 1987 with the Acorn Archimedes, introducing 
            a revolutionary RISC processor design that prioritized simplicity, efficiency, and power consumption. 
            What started as a British desktop computer processor became the foundation for virtually all mobile 
            devices today, powering billions of smartphones, tablets, and embedded systems worldwide.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-green-400">Key RISC Principles</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
            <li><strong>Simple instruction set:</strong> Only 27 core instructions in original ARM2</li>
            <li><strong>Load/store architecture:</strong> Memory accessed only through dedicated instructions</li>
            <li><strong>Register-rich design:</strong> 16 general-purpose 32-bit registers</li>
            <li><strong>Conditional execution:</strong> Every instruction can be conditionally executed</li>
            <li><strong>Uniform instruction format:</strong> All instructions are 32-bit aligned</li>
            <li><strong>Low power consumption:</strong> Designed for efficiency from the beginning</li>
          </ul>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-green-400">Revolutionary Design Features</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
            <li><strong>Barrel shifter:</strong> Built-in shifter for efficient bit manipulation</li>
            <li><strong>Pipeline optimization:</strong> Three-stage pipeline for maximum throughput</li>
            <li><strong>Condition codes:</strong> Every instruction can test processor flags</li>
            <li><strong>Flexible operands:</strong> Second operand can be shifted/rotated inline</li>
            <li><strong>Memory management:</strong> Clean virtual memory support</li>
          </ul>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-green-400">ARM Evolution</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>ARM2 (1987):</strong> Original 8MHz processor in Archimedes</li>
            <li><strong>ARM3 (1989):</strong> Added cache and higher clock speeds</li>
            <li><strong>ARM6 (1991):</strong> 32-bit architecture with MMU</li>
            <li><strong>ARM7 (1994):</strong> Thumb instruction set for code density</li>
            <li><strong>StrongARM (1995):</strong> High-performance implementation</li>
            <li><strong>ARM11 (2002):</strong> Out-of-order execution and SIMD</li>
            <li><strong>Cortex (2005+):</strong> Application, real-time, and microcontroller profiles</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6 text-white">Learning Path</h2>
        
        {silver.length > 0 && (
          <div class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>🥈</span>
              <span class="text-gray-300">Silver Tier - RISC Foundation (1,024 lessons each)</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              {silver.map(system => (
                <a href={`/systems/${system.slug}/`} class="block bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-800 hover:border-green-400 transition-all">
                  <div class="flex items-start justify-between mb-3">
                    <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">{system.data.name || system.data.title}</h4>
                    <MedalBadge tier={system.data.medal_tier} size="small" />
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-3">{system.data.year} • {system.data.manufacturer}</p>
                  <div class="flex gap-4 text-xs text-gray-500">
                    <span>{system.data.total_lessons} lessons</span>
                    <span>{system.data.total_games} games</span>
                  </div>
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        )}

        {gold.length > 0 && (
          <div class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>🥇</span>
              <span class="text-gray-300">Gold Tier - Advanced RISC (2,048 lessons each)</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              {gold.map(system => (
                <a href={`/systems/${system.slug}/`} class="block bg-gray-900 rounded-lg p-6 border-2 border-gray-800 hover:border-green-400 transition-all">
                  <div class="flex items-start justify-between mb-3">
                    <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">{system.data.name || system.data.title}</h4>
                    <MedalBadge tier={system.data.medal_tier} size="small" />
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-3">{system.data.year} • {system.data.manufacturer}</p>
                  <div class="flex gap-4 text-xs text-gray-500">
                    <span>{system.data.total_lessons} lessons</span>
                    <span>{system.data.total_games} games</span>
                    <span>{system.data.estimated_duration}</span>
                  </div>
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        )}
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-red-900 to-pink-900 rounded-lg p-8 border-2 border-red-700">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Recommended Learning Path</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-gray-300">
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="text-2xl">1️⃣</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Master RISC Fundamentals with Acorn Archimedes</h3>
              <p class="text-sm">Learn the elegant ARM assembly language and RISC OS programming. Understand the principles of RISC architecture, efficient instruction design, and how simplicity leads to performance.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="text-2xl">2️⃣</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Explore Advanced Graphics with Custom Chips</h3>
              <p class="text-sm">Master the VIDC graphics controller and understand how ARM systems efficiently handle multimedia. Learn graphics programming techniques that scale from desktop to mobile.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="text-2xl">3️⃣</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Understand Modular System Design</h3>
              <p class="text-sm">Explore RISC OS modules and dynamic linking concepts that influenced modern mobile operating systems. Learn clean software architecture principles.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="text-2xl">4️⃣</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Bridge to Modern ARM Development</h3>
              <p class="text-sm">Apply classic ARM knowledge to understanding modern smartphones, tablets, and embedded systems. See how 1987 innovations became today's mobile computing foundation.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-lg p-8 mt-8 border-2 border-gray-700">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Why Learn ARM Assembly?</h3>
        <div class="text-gray-300 space-y-3">
          <p>
            ARM assembly programming teaches the purest form of RISC computing concepts that power 
            today's mobile world. Unlike complex CISC processors, ARM's clean design makes it ideal 
            for learning fundamental computer architecture principles that remain relevant across all 
            modern computing platforms.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Acorn Archimedes introduced concepts in 1987 that became standard decades later: 
            efficient power usage, clean instruction sets, and multimedia acceleration. Understanding 
            these foundations provides deep insight into why ARM became dominant in mobile computing 
            and embedded systems.
          </p>
          <p>
            Programming the original ARM systems teaches optimization techniques, efficient algorithms, 
            and clean code practices that directly apply to modern development. The architectural 
            principles learned here scale from microcontrollers to supercomputers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>